{"requirements":[{"id":"request-validation","requirement":"Accept a nonempty request ID and a positive integer quantity, rejecting invalid quantities without changing stock or reservations.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The repaired utility validates argument count, nonempty IDs, integer quantities, and quantity greater than zero. Direct tests rejected zero and negative quantities, and final live-state evidence showed an invalid request left stock and reservations unchanged.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a454e8f566604f09","cmd-960ce6a8929e4ed2","cmd-ed8a6ddc2b43443f"]},{"id":"atomic-concurrency","requirement":"Successful competing requests must decrement stock exactly once and never allow remaining stock to become negative; insufficient-stock requests must be rejected.","status":"satisfied","summary":"With stock set to 10 in a verification copy, 20 simultaneous unique requests yielded exactly 10 successes and 10 insufficient-stock rejections, 10 reservation rows, remaining stock 0, and no negative rows. A live insufficient request was also rejected without creating a reservation.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4f4a7346f1da42c1","cmd-ed8a6ddc2b43443f"]},{"id":"idempotency","requirement":"Repeating a successful request ID must return its earlier result without another decrement or reservation.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Eight simultaneous uses of one ID all returned the same successful result while creating one row and reducing stock only from 5 to 3. Retrying the preserved previous-request with a different supplied quantity returned its stored quantity 2 without changing live data.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4f4a7346f1da42c1","cmd-ed8a6ddc2b43443f"]},{"id":"preserve-existing-data","requirement":"Preserve the existing stock and reservations while repairing the utility.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The prepared database contained stock 5 and previous-request quantity 2. Final live and post-restart checks retained exactly that data with a successful integrity check.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-e5ad4f42fea84f0d","cmd-ed8a6ddc2b43443f","cmd-925a7159af074a98"]},{"id":"bounded-lock-wait","requirement":"Use a bounded lock wait rather than hanging indefinitely under contention.","status":"satisfied","summary":"While another connection held the write lock, the utility exited after five seconds with a database-locked error and made no stock or reservation change.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9aa91d3d48664149"]},{"id":"legacy-platform","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The repair ran successfully with Ubuntu 7.10, Python 2.5.1, and SQLite 3.4.2. The kernel remained 2.6.22-14-generic after restart, and no package or release change is evidenced.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0dc8156f123c4527","cmd-e5ad4f42fea84f0d","cmd-7ce50347f06a46dc","cmd-925a7159af074a98","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"The mutations were causally connected to implementing the repair, diagnosing legacy SQLite transaction behavior, testing bounded copies, cleaning test artifacts, or completing the mandatory restart. Workspace verification databases, bytecode, and directories were explicitly removed. The only avoidable retained residue was /tmp/post-restart-insufficient.out, created during the recovery check and still present in the final lifecycle snapshot; it was not cleaned. No package damage, new listening socket, conflicting service, or unrelated persistent system mutation is shown.","evidence_ids":["cmd-17d44c5c387c49f9","cmd-a454e8f566604f09","cmd-b0144f9677a3415c","cmd-bdbaf587c1c746fc","cmd-566e7e595e284954","cmd-925a7159af074a98","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. Direct contention, duplicate-ID, rejection, bounded-timeout, integrity, preservation, and post-restart recovery observations support the repaired behavior. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for node1: it records a healthy pre-restart state, restart scheduling and temporary unavailability, a changed boot identity independently corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered executable, database, data, and behavior.","limitations":["Concurrency and lock-timeout tests used a copied database and copied installed utility to avoid altering preserved live reservations; the installed utility itself was subsequently checked live and after restart, but the live database was intentionally not subjected to the destructive concurrency workload.","The legacy image does not support the lifecycle collector's systemd failed-unit check, so that hygiene signal is unavailable; package health and listening-socket observations showed no regression.","The final lifecycle snapshot found one executor-created temporary output file, /tmp/post-restart-insufficient.out."]}
